.TH DICTATE 1 "2026-10-01" "dictate" "User Commands"
.SH NAME
dictate \- toggle voice dictation into the focused window
.SH SYNOPSIS
.B dictate
[\fIOPTIONS\fR]
.P
.B dictate
.B \-i
\fIFILE\fR
[\fB\-o\fR]
.SH DESCRIPTION
.B dictate
records from the microphone and transcribes speech locally with
.BR whisper-cli (1),
then types the result into whichever window currently has focus \- including
terminals, editors and browsers. The default mode is a toggle: the first
invocation starts recording, the next stops it, transcribes and types.
.P
Recording uses
.BR pw-record (1)
(PipeWire) at 16\ kHz mono; if
.B pw-record
is unavailable the script falls back to
.BR parec (1).
Text is injected with
.BR ydotool (1),
which sends real input events through
.IR /dev/uinput
and therefore works on Wayland compositors such as KWin that do not implement
the virtual-keyboard protocol used by
.BR wtype (1).
.P
Transcription is fully offline. The model is loaded from disk on every run, so
.B dictate
holds no memory while idle; only the small
.B ydotoold
daemon stays resident.
.SH OPTIONS
.TP
.BI \-i " FILE"
Transcribe
.I FILE
(WAV, MP3, and other formats whisper.cpp can read) and type the result,
instead of toggling the microphone.
.TP
.B \-o
Print the transcript to standard output instead of typing it.
.TP
.BI \-m " FILE"
Path to the whisper model. Default:
.IR ~/.local/share/whisper/models/ggml-large-v3-turbo-q5_0.bin .
.TP
.BI \-l " LANG"
Spoken language as an ISO code (en, de, ...), or
.B auto
to detect it. Default:
.IR en .
.TP
.BI \-d " DEV"
Capture device or PipeWire target node. Default: the system default source.
.TP
.BI \-t " N"
Number of threads passed to
.BR whisper-cli .
Default: the number of CPUs
.RB ( nproc ).
.TP
.B \-h
Show a short help message and exit.
.SH BEHAVIOUR
.SS State
Toggle state lives in
.IR $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dictate- N ,
where
.I N
is the user id. The recorder's PID is stored in
.I rec.pid
and the audio in
.IR rec.wav .
An
.BR flock (1)
lock stops two toggles from racing.
.SS Transcript cleanup
Non-speech tags emitted by whisper (for example
.B [BLANK_AUDIO]
or
.BR (silence) )
are removed, newlines are collapsed to spaces, and surrounding whitespace is
trimmed. No trailing newline or
.B Enter
key is inserted, so the text can be reviewed before it is sent.
.SS Typing speed
The transcript is typed with
.BR ydotool .
The inter-key delay and hold default to 8\ ms (faster than ydotool's own
20\ ms); raise
.B DICTATE_KEY_DELAY
and
.B DICTATE_KEY_HOLD
if a busy application drops characters.
.SS Notifications
Progress is reported by desktop notifications through
.BR notify-send (1):
recording, transcribing, inserted, or an error.
.SS Requirements
.IP \(bu 2
.B whisper-cli
and a ggml model (package
.BR whisper-cpp ).
.IP \(bu 2
.B ydotool
with the
.B ydotoold
user service running, for typing.
.IP \(bu 2
.B pw-record
(PipeWire) or
.BR parec .
.SH ENVIRONMENT
These variables set the defaults; the matching command-line options override
them.
.TP
.B DICTATE_MODEL
Path to the whisper model (see
.BR \-m ).
.TP
.B DICTATE_LANG
Spoken language (see
.BR \-l ).
.TP
.B DICTATE_DEVICE
Capture device (see
.BR \-d ).
.TP
.B DICTATE_THREADS
Number of whisper threads. Default:
.BR nproc .
.TP
.B DICTATE_KEY_DELAY
Milliseconds between typed keys, passed to
.BR ydotool .
Default: 8.
.TP
.B DICTATE_KEY_HOLD
Milliseconds each key is held, passed to
.BR ydotool .
Default: 8.
.SH EXAMPLES
Toggle dictation (bind this to a global shortcut):
.IP
.EX
dictate
.EE
.P
Transcribe a file and print it:
.IP
.EX
dictate \-i interview.wav \-o
.EE
.P
Transcribe a file and type it into the focused window:
.IP
.EX
dictate \-i note.mp3
.EE
.P
Use a smaller, faster model:
.IP
.EX
dictate \-m ~/.local/share/whisper/models/ggml-small.en.bin
.EE
.SH EXIT STATUS
.TP
.B 0
Success, including the "no speech detected" and "no audio captured" cases.
.TP
.B 1
Failure: a dependency is missing, the model is absent, or another
.B dictate
run already holds the lock.
.TP
.B 2
Usage error (unknown option or missing argument).
.SH FILES
.TP
.I ~/.local/share/whisper/models/
Default model directory.
.TP
.I $XDG_RUNTIME_DIR/dictate- N /
Runtime state: PID file, recorded WAV and lock.
.SH SEE ALSO
.BR whisper-cli (1),
.BR ydotool (1),
.BR ydotoold (8),
.BR pw-record (1),
.BR parec (1),
.BR notify-send (1)
.SH BUGS
Text is typed into whatever window has focus at the moment transcription
finishes; do not trigger it while a password or other secure prompt is focused.
The cleanup pass also removes any real parentheses or brackets that whisper
produces verbatim.
.SH AUTHOR
Written for local use.
